A task management system is a digital tool that helps individuals and teams plan, assign, track, and organize their work from start to finish.
Key features of task managenment:
Task Creation and Assignment:Break down projects into actionable steps and assign an owner to each task.
Prioritization and Deadlines: Set due dates and sort tasks by urgency so everyone knows what to tackle first.
Visual Workflows: Use boards, lists, or calendars (like Kanban views) to see task stages at a glance (e.g., To Do, In Progress, Done).
Real-Time Collaboration: Share files, leave comments, and get automated notifications without needing status-update meetings.
Progress Tracking: Monitor overall team performance and spot bottlenecks early.
